Source: homelab-dns-server
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab-api

Package: homelab-dns-server
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, pdns-server, pdns-backend-pgsql, postgresql-client, adduser
Description: PowerDNS authoritative DNS provisioning for Homelab
 Wires PowerDNS's PostgreSQL (gpgsql) backend via the native pdns.d
 drop-in directory -- never edits pdns.conf directly. Supports the real
 master/slave topology (one master, N slaves) already in use. Applies
 the official upstream schema (referenced from the installed
 pdns-backend-pgsql package, not vendored/duplicated) only if it isn't
 already present, and never touches any other tenant of the same
 database (e.g. a DKIM key-management table living alongside it).
